    "campaign": "Fresh Market",
    "caption": "Take a breather from your busy day and sit down to this Chicken Teriyaki Lettuce Wrap that’s fresh, light, and savory.\n\nMade with Magnolia Chicken Breast, these lettuce wraps are easy to prepare. Make them in advance to take with you to the office (just pack the meat and lettuce in separate containers and assemble before you indulge) or enjoy at the comfort of home. Find all the ingredients you need for this recipe at #TheMarketplace!\n\nServing Time: 40 minutes\nYield: 4-5 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n2 pcs. Magnolia Chicken Breast\n3 cloves garlic \n3 slices ginger \nSalt and pepper to taste\n¾ cup water\n¼ cup soy sauce\n¼ cup sugar\n½ tsp. ginger powder\n½ tsp. garlic powder\n3 tbsps. cornstarch slurry\n1 tsp. sesame oil\n2 tbsps. Canola oil\n12 pcs. romaine lettuce\n1 cup carrots, julienned\n½ cup onions, julienned\n¼ cup scallions, sliced\n2 tbsps. sesame seeds\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Add Magnolia Chicken Breast, garlic and ginger into a pot filled with water, then season with salt and pepper. Let simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n2. Remove chicken breast from the pot, and let cool. Once cooled, shred and set aside.\n3. In a small saucepan, add in water, soy sauce, sugar, ginger powder and garlic powder. Mix and place over medium heat. Once simmering, add in cornstarch slurry, and cook until thickened. Remove from the heat, then mix in sesame oil.\n4. Set a pan over medium heat. Add in canola oil, and fry shredded chicken until lightly browned. Mix in prepared teriyaki sauce, and toss to coat the chicken.\n5. To assemble, fill romaine lettuce with coated shredded chicken, carrots and onions. Garnish with scallions and sesame seeds.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
