    "campaign": "Fresh Market",
    "caption": "Hailing from Japan, Omurice is a dish comprising of an omelette with fried rice that’s usually made with leftovers. It’s a hearty and comforting dish that’s simple to prepare yet bursting with so much flavor.\n\nUsing Bounty Fresh Omega-3 Enriched Specialty Eggs for that richer, eggier taste, we made this omurice in around half an hour using ingredients that you can simply find at home. Try making it for your next meal. If you’re missing some ingredients, #TheMarketplace is just around the corner to help replenish your supplies. \n\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 1-2 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n3 tbsps. canola oil\n1 white onion, diced\n2 cups day-old rice\n1 cup frozen mixed vegetables\n1 tbsp. soy sauce\n½ cup ketchup\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 tbsp. butter\n3 pcs Bounty Fresh Omega-3 Enriched Specialty Eggs\n1 tbsp. dashi stock\n1 tbsp. scallions, sliced\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Set a wok over medium heat, then add in 2 tbsps. canola oil. Sauté white onions until translucent, then add in day-old rice. \n2. Mix in mixed vegetables, add soy sauce and 3 tbsps. ketchup. Season with salt and pepper, then finish off with butter. \n3. In a bowl, whisk together Bounty Fresh Omega-3 Enriched Specialty Eggs, dashi stock and salt. \n4. Set non-stick pan over low heat, and add the remaining canola oil. Add in beaten eggs, and move around with a spatula to avoid big curds. Continue to cook until mostly set, but center is still jammy.  \n5. Shape the rice using a round bowl, then turn over onto a serving plate. Top with the cooked omelette, then drizzle with the remaining ketchup on top. Garnish with scallions.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
