    "categoryConfidence": "medium",
    "campaign": "Fresh Market",
    "caption": "Make this impressive Orange Cranberry Pound Cake with Sunnyphil Seedless Size 88 Oranges!\n\nBursting with the citrusy goodness of oranges and juicy cranberries, this loaf is perfect to snack on during your afternoon tea-time, or to make ahead and freeze. Nothing beats a labor of love, and this pound cake is also great to gift to loved ones. Head over to #TheMarketplace to get the freshest oranges and all the other ingredients that you need for this recipe.\n\nServing Time: 1 hour and 30 minutes\nYield: 8x4-inch loaf\n\nIngredients\n\n½ cup butter\n1⅓ cup sugar\n3 eggs\n1½ cup flour, sifted\n1 tsp. baking powder\n½ tsp. salt\n½ cup sour cream\n½ tbsp. vanilla extract\n2 tbsps. orange zest\n1 cup frozen cranberries\n¾ cup powdered sugar, sifted\n1 tbsp. heavy cream\n1 tbsp. orange juice\n½ cup Sunnyphil Seedless Orange Size 88, slices\n1 tbsp. thyme\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Preheat oven to 175°C. Line a 8x4-inch loaf pan with parchment paper. \n2. In a large bowl, whisk together flour, baking powder and salt. Set aside.\n3. Using a stand mixer fitted with the paddle attachment, cream butter and sugar until pale and fluffy. With the mixer on low, add the eggs one at a time, making sure each one is well combined before adding the next. Add in the flour mixture gradually. Mix in sour cream, vanilla extract and orange zest. \n4. By hand, fold in ¾ cup frozen cranberry.\n5. Transfer to the lined loaf pan, and bake for 50-60 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Let cool.\n6. In a bowl, whisk together powdered sugar, heavy cream, and orange juice.\n7. Pour the glaze over the cooled cake, then top with Sunnyphil Seedless Orange Size 88 slices, remaining cranberries and thyme.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
