    "caption": "Have a special gathering coming up home? Drop by #TheMarketplace and grab a rack of our fresh Imported Baby Back Ribs and marinate in a special homemade sauce. To bring out the ribs’ best flavor, let them sit overnight with the sauce before chucking them into the oven. Serve with your choice of sides and don’t forget to pair with a fine bottle of red wine! Your guests will surely love it.\n\nServing Time: 5 hours\nYield: 4-5 servings\nTips: Marinate overnight for best flavor\n\nIngredients\n\n2 tbsps. garlic, grated\n1 tbsp. ginger, grated\n2 tbsps. shallots, minced\n⅓ cup soy sauce\n3 tbsps. fish sauce\n¼ cup lime juice\n4 tbsps. brown sugar\n½ tbsp. black pepper\n1 rack Imported Baby Back Ribs\n2 stalks lemongrass, crushed\n½ cup cilantro\n⅛ cup roasted peanuts, chopped\n3 tbsps. red chilies, chopped\n1 pc. lime, sliced into wedges\n\nProcedure\n\n1. In a bowl, combine garlic, ginger, shallots, soy sauce, fish sauce, lime juice, brown sugar and black pepper.\n2. Place the Imported Baby Back Ribs in a large container, along with the lemongrass. Pour over prepared marinade, and spread to fully coat the ribs. Cover and marinate for at least 1 hour or overnight.\n3. Preheat oven to 175°C. Line a large baking tray with foil. \n4. Transfer the ribs onto the lined baking tray, then cover with foil. Bake for 2-3 hours, or until fork tender.\n5. Remove the foil cover, then broil for another 30 minutes. \n6. Garnish with cilantro, roasted peanuts and red chili. Serve with lime wedges. \n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
